Phoenix Print Farm is a sovereign, autonomous manufacturing system designed to replace centralized factories, overseas supply chains, and physical inventory with localized, software-defined production.

The system operates on digital inventory, producing parts on demand from verified design files. Manufacturing occurs only when authorized, ensuring traceability, resilience, and national control over production capacity.

Phoenix Print Farms are built for continuous, unattended operation using high-speed multi-material 3D printing cells. Throughput scales horizontally by adding print cells rather than facilities, enabling rapid deployment in urban, rural, and disaster-response environments.

This repository defines the architecture, operations, security, governance, and supply chain model for Phoenix Print Farm deployments.

This repository is architecture-first. It defines standards, control models, and deployment frameworks rather than application code.
